'''theina''' (thē-ī′nä), ''n.'' Same as ''theine''.

'''theine''' (thē′in), ''n.'' [< NL. ''theina'', ''thea'', tea.] A bitter crystallizable volatile principle (C<sub>8</sub>H<sub>10</sub>N<sub>4</sub>O<sub>2</sub>) found in tea, coffee, and some other plants, tea yielding from 2 to 4 per cent. {{smaller|It is considered to be the principle which gives to tea its refreshing and gently stimulating qualities: same as ''caffein''.}}

